  "description_short": "Garden-based kiosk serving fresh breakfast and light meals in George's scenic Van Riebeek Gardens.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the leafy Van Riebeek Gardens in Heatherlands, Trail Kiosk @ Ground Zero offers a relaxed spot for breakfast and light meals among the trees. The setting is casual and green, popular with walkers, trail runners, and families looking for a bite after exploring the gardens.\n\nThe menu keeps things simple with breakfast staples, fresh sandwiches, wraps, and coffee. It's the kind of place where you grab a table under the shade, watch the kids play nearby, and enjoy uncomplicated food in a peaceful garden setting. Service is laid-back and the vibe is community-focused — locals drop in regularly.\n\nLocated in George's quieter neighbourhoods, it's an easy stop if you're heading to or from the garden trails. Whether you're fuelling up before a walk or winding down with a coffee afterwards, Trail Kiosk fits the bill without any fuss.",
